[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4958434890","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/121300#issuecomment-4958434890","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121300","id":4958434890,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABJ4u2Sg","user":{"login":"Arecher","id":10502115,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNTAyMTE1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10502115?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher","html_url":"https://github.com/Arecher","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-13T13:26:11Z","updated_at":"2026-07-13T15:33:06Z","body":"I wondered about this, since I have been using shaders and shader includes in 4.7 extensively, and for me declaring a `uniform float shaderinclude_uniform;` seems to work fine.\n\n<img width=\"546\" height=\"151\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c071db5e-8a83-43e8-a605-7160f6a245e7\" />\n\nThey show up at the top, because the `#include` declarations in the main shader are above the other uniforms. The only oddity I ran into was that declaring a `group_uniforms shaderinclude_uniforms` includes the uniforms from all shaderincludes, rather than only the ones that are within the file that has the `group_uniforms` declaration (in my case the group was declared in `math.gdshaderinc` but also includes uniforms from `masks.gdshaderinc`. It feels like it would make more sense for the group to end at the end of the file, but I presume this parsing only happens **after** the include files are merged into the main file.\n\nSo there must be something more specific to this. What type of uniforms where they? How and where were they declared? Where are the `#includes` declared in the main shader?\n\nAre they perhaps `instance uniform` declarations, in which case they might be found on the Mesh, rather than the shadermaterial.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4958434890/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5039075920","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/121300#issuecomment-5039075920","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121300","id":5039075920,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABLFoyUA","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-21T21:09:27Z","updated_at":"2026-07-21T21:09:27Z","body":"I can't reproduce this on 4.8 aac1c92f5 (Linux):\n\n<img width=\"1911\" height=\"1076\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c11beca2-5219-43be-82fe-ec116be77a99\" />\n\n`new_shader_include.gdshaderinc` contains just `uniform int from_include = 123;`.\n\n@mikest Please upload a minimal reproduction project[^1] to make this easier to troubleshoot.\n\n[^1]: A small Godot project which reproduces the issue, with no unnecessary files included. Be sure to not include the `.godot` folder in the archive (but keep `project.godot`).<br><br>Drag and drop a ZIP archive to upload it. **Do not select another field until the project is done uploading.**<br><br>**Note for C# users:** If your issue is *not* C#-specific, please upload a minimal reproduction project written in GDScript. This will make it easier for contributors to reproduce the issue locally as not everyone has a Mono setup available. ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5039075920/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5040517148","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/121300#issuecomment-5040517148","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121300","id":5040517148,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABLHAwHA","user":{"login":"mikest","id":742517,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc0MjUxNw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/742517?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikest","html_url":"https://github.com/mikest","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikest/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikest/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikest/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikest/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikest/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikest/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-22T00:37:22Z","updated_at":"2026-07-22T00:37:22Z","body":"The shader is here:\nhttps://github.com/mikest/halyard/blob/ce0eafaf7bb5f22b0ee7ab879c4b62784cf8dbe7/shaders/ocean_shader.gdshader\n\nLine 69 includes a `wind.gdshaderinc`\n\nThe include is here:\nhttps://github.com/mikest/halyard/blob/ce0eafaf7bb5f22b0ee7ab879c4b62784cf8dbe7/shaders/wind.gdshaderinc\n\nThere is a define switch\n`#define GLOBAL_WIND` that switches between global and local uniforms. Toggle this flag to see the behavior.\n\nWhen global uniforms are used, they don't show up in the editor. Note the inclusion/exclusion of the \"Wind\" group in the side panel.\n\n<img width=\"1624\" height=\"972\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ed30cd7c-3e4f-4283-bd47-cc986b830335\" />\n<img width=\"1624\" height=\"972\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d1e47f8e-f91b-4d50-867c-cd6f2a429ef5\" />\n\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5040517148/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5040546628","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/121300#issuecomment-5040546628","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121300","id":5040546628,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABLHCjRA","user":{"login":"mikest","id":742517,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc0MjUxNw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/742517?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikest","html_url":"https://github.com/mikest","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikest/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikest/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikest/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikest/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikest/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikest/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-22T00:42:33Z","updated_at":"2026-07-22T00:42:33Z","body":"For an MRP:\n\n1. this repo can be checked out directly into a new project addons folder:\nhttps://github.com/mikest/halyard/\n2. add the global uniforms in the debug output to the project shader globals.\n3. build with scons\n4. open the `examples/ocean_area.tscn`\n5.  open node OceanArea > Properties: WaveSampler >Material\n6. open res://addons/halyard/shaders/wind.gdshaderinc\n\n7. Comment/uncomment line 9","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5040546628/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5040608738","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/121300#issuecomment-5040608738","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121300","id":5040608738,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABLHGV4g","user":{"login":"mikest","id":742517,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc0MjUxNw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/742517?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikest","html_url":"https://github.com/mikest","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikest/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikest/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikest/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikest/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikest/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikest/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-22T00:53:43Z","updated_at":"2026-07-22T00:53:43Z","body":"(I will see if I can make this more minimal, with fewer steps.)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5040608738/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5042770139","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/121300#issuecomment-5042770139","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121300","id":5042770139,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABLJKQ2w","user":{"login":"Arecher","id":10502115,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNTAyMTE1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10502115?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher","html_url":"https://github.com/Arecher","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-22T06:46:13Z","updated_at":"2026-07-22T06:48:47Z","body":"It seems to be specifically `global uniform` declarations that do not show up, regardless of whether they are in an include file or not.\n\nI'm unsure if that's intended behaviour or not, since the [documentation](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.html#global-uniforms) specifically states that:\n\n> While you can assign a default value using global uniform vec4 my_color = ... in the shader code, it will be ignored as the global uniform must always be defined in the Project Settings anyway.\n\nIf assigning a value (through editor or as default) means it gets overwritten, there is little to gain from it being editable/shown in the editor.\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5042770139/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5047001006","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/121300#issuecomment-5047001006","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121300","id":5047001006,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABLNMfrg","user":{"login":"mikest","id":742517,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc0MjUxNw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/742517?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikest","html_url":"https://github.com/mikest","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikest/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikest/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikest/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikest/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikest/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikest/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-22T14:02:37Z","updated_at":"2026-07-22T14:02:37Z","body":"The shader panel should show them and allow them to be edited, acting on the global values. There's very little reason to require to the user to run out to the Project settings for this and doing so is cumbersome.\n\nHowever, it appears as if they have never been shown and I was confused about the original behavior when I wrote this bug. It should probably be a feature request instead.\n\nApologies.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5047001006/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]